WEBVTT

00:08.980 --> 00:11.414
First box goes in my car,
the other in the truck.

00:14.319 --> 00:15.684
Guess that's it.

00:16.187 --> 00:18.314
- You got everything?
- I think so.

00:18.490 --> 00:22.221
I left the house keys and
the garage clicker by the nightstand.

00:22.660 --> 00:24.218
Thanks.

00:24.396 --> 00:27.058
So you still planning
to move in with your dad?

00:27.232 --> 00:28.665
Just for a while.

00:28.833 --> 00:32.166
- You gonna be okay?
- Me? Oh, yeah. Yeah.

00:32.337 --> 00:34.737
I mean, I am gonna miss the cat.

00:35.040 --> 00:36.337
You hate Sir Lancelot.

00:36.775 --> 00:39.073
I did at first,
but over time I came to find...

00:39.244 --> 00:41.872
Yeah, you're right, I hate that thing.

00:42.447 --> 00:44.847
I put in a change of address
at the post office...

00:45.016 --> 00:47.143
...but here's my address just in case.

00:47.318 --> 00:48.717
I might be open to a trade.

00:48.887 --> 00:50.548
I'll keep the cat, you take Alan.

00:51.489 --> 00:53.354
Still got his carrier.

00:53.792 --> 00:56.454
- Take care of yourself, Charlie.
- You do the same.

01:01.232 --> 01:02.631
I'm sorry it didn't work out.

01:04.002 --> 01:05.560
Me too.

01:14.846 --> 01:17.041
Well, she's gone.

01:17.415 --> 01:18.939
You handled that very maturely.

01:19.384 --> 01:21.113
What are you gonna do?

01:21.286 --> 01:24.653
We tried, it didn't work. Life goes on.

01:24.823 --> 01:25.881
You want a drink?

01:26.057 --> 01:28.321
No, drinking isn't gonna
solve anything.

01:30.895 --> 01:32.123
What are you doing?

01:32.297 --> 01:33.559
Nothing.

01:33.731 --> 01:36.564
Really? Doesn't look like nothing.

01:37.135 --> 01:38.159
Where you going?

01:39.737 --> 01:41.466
Out for a swim.

01:41.673 --> 01:43.072
You never go in the water.

01:43.241 --> 01:45.732
That's because
I'm not a good swimmer.

01:47.712 --> 01:50.977
- You don't think he's gonna...
- I don't know.

01:51.749 --> 01:54.217
Charlie? Charlie, stop this!

01:54.385 --> 01:56.615
Charlie, come back, it's not that bad!

01:56.788 --> 01:58.949
Come on, Charlie,
you still got your family!

01:59.124 --> 02:01.922
Very smart, now he's sprinting.

02:02.627 --> 02:05.790
Damn it, Charlie, get out of that water!

02:05.964 --> 02:07.363
We need to go after him.

02:07.532 --> 02:10.660
Well, don't look at me.
I just ate, I gotta wait a half an hour.

02:10.835 --> 02:13.827
I just washed my hair
and this is leave-in conditioner.

02:14.005 --> 02:15.870
- What about Jake?
- At his mother's.

02:16.040 --> 02:18.167
- Maybe we should give him a call.
- There's no time.

02:18.877 --> 02:22.244
Water's really cold.

02:23.281 --> 02:26.808
Just so you know,
we were about to come get you.

02:56.915 --> 02:58.610
Charlie?

02:59.851 --> 03:01.341
You awake?

03:02.720 --> 03:06.281
Come on, man, it's time to get up.

03:11.029 --> 03:12.724
Charlie?

03:14.465 --> 03:16.456
- What?
- Aah!

03:20.705 --> 03:22.639
I didn't see you there.

03:23.474 --> 03:26.136
She was the best thing
that ever happened to me, Alan.

03:26.544 --> 03:29.672
I understand,
but you've been up here for two days.

03:30.348 --> 03:32.111
It's time to move on with your life.

03:32.283 --> 03:34.444
There's no life to move on with.

03:34.619 --> 03:35.745
Well, sure there is.

03:35.954 --> 03:40.152
You've got money, a beautiful home,
good looks, all your hair...

03:40.325 --> 03:43.522
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
I have all the things you don't.

03:43.695 --> 03:47.529
That wasn't really the point
I was trying to make, but, uh...

03:48.866 --> 03:50.493
Come on.

03:50.668 --> 03:51.726
Come on.

03:51.903 --> 03:55.168
- Where are we going?
- We are going to get you cleaned up.

03:55.340 --> 03:57.672
No. No, I can't go in there.

03:57.842 --> 03:59.503
It reminds me too much of Chelsea.

04:00.044 --> 04:01.068
The bathroom?

04:01.246 --> 04:04.943
That's where she used to brush her hair
and floss her teeth...

04:05.116 --> 04:07.243
...and tinkle like a princess.

04:08.686 --> 04:11.314
Okay, well,
where have you been tinkling?

04:13.992 --> 04:16.517
I may need a new ficus.

04:19.931 --> 04:21.956
I'm glad you came with me.

04:22.600 --> 04:24.500
You needed to get out of the house.

04:24.669 --> 04:27.661
No, what I need is to be loved again.

04:27.839 --> 04:32.902
Uh, well, I think a good first step
is to stop urinating in the potted plants.

04:34.145 --> 04:36.841
Jake, your dad's here.

04:37.515 --> 04:41.110
Charlie, I was so sorry
to hear about you and Chelsea.

04:41.286 --> 04:42.412
Thank you.

04:42.820 --> 04:46.278
I know that breakups
can be very difficult.

04:46.457 --> 04:48.925
Unless you're kicking out
your husband of 12 years.

04:49.093 --> 04:50.720
That seemed remarkably easy.

04:50.895 --> 04:52.260
It was.

04:54.399 --> 04:57.391
You know the part
that I don't understand, Judith...

04:57.568 --> 05:00.230
...is how somebody can tell you
they love you one day...

05:00.405 --> 05:03.465
...then turn around
and break your heart the next.

05:03.641 --> 05:07.099
Well, relationships are complicated.
People drift apart.

05:07.278 --> 05:10.270
- Nobody's to blame.
- You blamed me.

05:10.448 --> 05:11.813
It was your fault.

05:13.718 --> 05:18.178
I tried to change, tried to become
the man she wanted me to be...

05:18.356 --> 05:19.618
...but it wasn't enough.

05:20.258 --> 05:23.750
Oh, I'm sure there's a part of her
that still loves you very much.

05:24.362 --> 05:26.330
There a part of you that still loves me?

05:26.497 --> 05:27.623
No.

05:30.702 --> 05:31.999
What's wrong with him?

05:32.170 --> 05:34.229
Your uncle's very upset
about his breakup.

05:34.772 --> 05:35.796
Oh, yeah, that sucks.

05:35.973 --> 05:37.804
Can I drive?

05:37.975 --> 05:39.272
- Sure.
- Cool.

05:39.444 --> 05:41.469
Let's go, crybaby.

05:53.157 --> 05:54.351
Hi.

05:54.525 --> 05:57.153
Yeah, hey, kind of busy here.

05:58.129 --> 05:59.289
I can see that.

05:59.464 --> 06:01.955
- Hi, I'm Jake's Uncle Charlie.
- Nicole.

06:02.133 --> 06:05.296
What's the deal, Nicole,
are you tutoring our little genius here?

06:05.837 --> 06:07.099
No, we're dating.

06:07.271 --> 06:09.831
- Oh. Dating?
- Uncle Charlie?

06:10.007 --> 06:11.634
Hang on.

06:12.477 --> 06:16.004
Listen, Nicole, I love this kid
and I don't wanna see him get hurt.

06:16.347 --> 06:18.542
- I'm not gonna hurt him.
- Oh, really?

06:18.716 --> 06:21.480
You like him the way he is?
You don't wanna change him?

06:21.819 --> 06:24.686
- Uncle Charlie...
- I got your back here, buddy.

06:26.457 --> 06:29.654
Because let me tell you something.
This, here, is a lump of clay.

06:31.195 --> 06:33.857
You know what it's gonna
be five, 10, 20 years from now?

06:34.031 --> 06:36.727
A larger, more bitter lump of clay.

06:36.901 --> 06:38.334
- Come on, let's go.
- Whoa, whoa.

06:38.503 --> 06:39.993
Whoa, I'm not done.

06:40.171 --> 06:42.036
If you're gonna dump him,
dump him now.

06:42.206 --> 06:46.142
Don't wait till he falls in love, asks you
to marry him and have his children.

06:47.945 --> 06:49.845
Okay, enjoy yourselves.

06:54.252 --> 06:55.879
Are you out of your mind?

06:56.554 --> 06:58.021
I mean well.

06:59.457 --> 07:02.551
- Maybe it's time to go to your shrink.
- She's another woman...

07:02.727 --> 07:05.355
...that wants to change me.
- You have to do something.

07:05.530 --> 07:07.521
No. No.

07:07.765 --> 07:09.858
If I can't have Chelsea,
I don't wanna live.

07:10.034 --> 07:12.969
- Where you going?
- Strip club.

07:15.039 --> 07:17.701
Ah, yes, death by lap dance.

07:46.637 --> 07:49.800
Hey, Lord, it's Charlie.

07:49.974 --> 07:54.001
I know it seems like I only call on you
when my ass is on fire.

07:54.212 --> 07:58.239
But, well, let's face it,
that's how you made me.

07:59.016 --> 08:03.146
Anyway, I'm just hurting
real bad since Chelsea left...

08:03.321 --> 08:05.789
...and I was kind of hoping
that maybe you could...

08:05.957 --> 08:08.016
...take away some of that pain.

08:08.226 --> 08:11.787
Even with the help of your blessed wine,
I can't get through the day.

08:11.963 --> 08:14.830
Even your blessed vodka's
stopped working.

08:15.600 --> 08:20.299
So anything you can do
would be much appreciated.

08:20.838 --> 08:21.964
Hey.

08:22.139 --> 08:24.437
You got a light?

08:24.976 --> 08:28.309
I like a little buzz before I pray.
Gets me closer to God.

08:29.847 --> 08:31.747
Thanks.

08:38.356 --> 08:40.688
Come on, Charlie, answer the phone.

08:40.858 --> 08:42.689
Oh, damn it, voicemail.

08:42.860 --> 08:45.488
Uh, Charlie, it's me again.
It has been three days.

08:45.663 --> 08:48.154
Please call
and let us know you're okay.

08:49.534 --> 08:51.661
- I think we should call the police.
- No, he'll turn up.

08:52.036 --> 08:54.027
May be broke and riddled
with gonorrhea...

08:54.205 --> 08:55.832
...but he'll find his way home.

08:56.007 --> 08:58.567
No, I don't think
this is a typical bender.

08:58.743 --> 09:00.074
He really cared for Chelsea.

09:00.545 --> 09:02.206
You know, he put her in his will.

09:03.014 --> 09:05.312
Anything happens to him,
she gets everything.

09:05.483 --> 09:08.077
Really? So like if he swam out
in the ocean...

09:08.252 --> 09:10.584
...and drowned, for instance,
she gets the house?

09:11.188 --> 09:14.419
The house, the Mercedes,
the bank accounts, the music royalties.

09:14.592 --> 09:16.150
Man, I just can't catch a break.

09:18.763 --> 09:21.493
Hey, look what someone threw away.

09:22.533 --> 09:25.001
Put that back outside.
And wash your hands.

09:27.505 --> 09:29.268
Welcome to your new home, baby.

09:32.510 --> 09:33.704
Hey, everybody.

09:33.878 --> 09:36.745
I want you to meet the love of my life,
Mrs. Charlie Harper.

09:39.083 --> 09:42.177
Better put me down.
I'm not wearing panties.

09:42.753 --> 09:45.847
I told you he'd come home
with gonorrhea.

09:46.457 --> 09:48.516
All right, who's who?

09:48.693 --> 09:51.389
Well, this is my brother Alan.
Alan, Betsy.

09:51.562 --> 09:53.359
Hello, brother.

09:54.031 --> 09:56.295
- Call me Alan.
- Okay.

09:56.467 --> 09:58.731
He doesn't look like such a mooch.

09:59.370 --> 10:01.133
Okay, well, this is my mom, Evelyn...

10:01.305 --> 10:03.967
...and she doesn't look
like such an Antichrist.

10:04.442 --> 10:05.568
Hi, Mom.

10:06.944 --> 10:08.741
Call me Mrs. Harper.

10:10.314 --> 10:12.908
- This is my housekeeper, Berta.
- Don't call me at all.

10:14.118 --> 10:15.745
And lastly, this is Jake.

10:17.121 --> 10:19.385
Oh, are you my son?

10:20.458 --> 10:22.824
I'll be whatever you want me to be.

10:25.062 --> 10:28.156
- Actually, he's my son.
- Butt out, Dad.

10:28.599 --> 10:31.124
Well, you've met everybody.

10:31.302 --> 10:33.793
Why don't we go upstairs
and continue the honeymoon?

10:33.971 --> 10:36.769
- We have got an upstairs?
Yep.

10:37.308 --> 10:40.141
Are there people up here too?

10:43.581 --> 10:45.412
I like her.

10:50.154 --> 10:51.678
- Hey, Dad?
- Mm-hm.

10:52.123 --> 10:54.819
Do I call Uncle Charlie's new wife
Betsy or Aunt Betsy?

10:54.992 --> 10:56.653
I guess either one's okay.

10:56.827 --> 10:59.955
- I'm gonna go with Aunt Betsy.
- Fine.

11:00.131 --> 11:02.929
Aunt Betsy made
a lot of noise last night.

11:04.101 --> 11:05.466
Uh, yeah. Yeah, she did.

11:05.636 --> 11:08.298
Don't get me wrong,
I'm not complaining.

11:10.107 --> 11:11.699
Good morning, family.

11:11.876 --> 11:13.343
Morning.
- How we doing today?

11:13.511 --> 11:15.172
- Good.
- Good.

11:15.346 --> 11:19.180
Will Aunt Betsy be joining us
or is she taking a hot, soapy shower?

11:20.284 --> 11:21.342
She'll be right down.

11:23.120 --> 11:25.350
So based on
this latest turn of events...

11:25.523 --> 11:28.686
...would it be fair to say
you're over Chelsea?

11:29.393 --> 11:31.554
Oh, absolutely.

11:31.762 --> 11:33.559
Betsy and I are soul mates.

11:33.764 --> 11:35.231
Soul mates? Uh-huh.

11:35.399 --> 11:38.334
- So, where'd you meet your soul mate?
- Guess.

11:39.203 --> 11:41.728
- Strip club?
- Wrong.

11:42.873 --> 11:45.535
- Massage parlor?
- Wrong.

11:46.911 --> 11:48.242
Okay, I give up.

11:48.412 --> 11:51.210
Betsy and I met in church.

11:51.382 --> 11:52.576
So, what, she's a nun?

11:53.084 --> 11:55.848
No, she's a stripper
and part-time masseuse.

11:56.487 --> 11:59.479
See, I drove to the strip club,
but the parking lot was full...

11:59.657 --> 12:01.887
...so I circled the block
looking for a spot...

12:02.059 --> 12:05.028
...and found one right in front
of this little church.

12:05.196 --> 12:07.892
For some reason, I don't know why,
I got out of my car...

12:08.065 --> 12:09.999
...walked into church, started praying.

12:10.167 --> 12:13.068
- Are you saying God sent you Betsy?
- I think he did.

12:13.237 --> 12:15.865
Oh, Dad, we gotta get our asses
to church.

12:17.608 --> 12:19.769
Then when I'm done,
I get up to leave...

12:19.944 --> 12:24.176
...and she appears in front of me
like some kind of vanilla-scented angel.

12:24.482 --> 12:26.245
Mm, vanilla.

12:26.817 --> 12:30.583
So we get to talking, turns out she's
going through a difficult time as well.

12:30.755 --> 12:34.589
Next thing, we're cleaning out her locker
at the club and driving to Vegas.

12:35.025 --> 12:36.549
Where you got married.

12:37.261 --> 12:40.753
I understand your skepticism,
but I'm telling you, this girl is special.

12:40.931 --> 12:43.297
She's really sweet and spiritual.

12:43.467 --> 12:46.265
Charlie?
- In here, baby.

12:46.871 --> 12:48.031
Good news, bad news.

12:48.205 --> 12:49.968
I got my period.

12:50.141 --> 12:52.234
Oh, that's okay. We can take a break.

12:52.409 --> 12:53.433
We don't have to.

12:53.611 --> 12:55.977
There's more than one way
to skin a cat.

12:56.981 --> 12:59.541
Oh, you are so wonderful.

12:59.984 --> 13:02.817
- What are the other ways?
- Shh. Uh...

13:02.987 --> 13:05.080
Can I talk to you in private
for a minute?

13:05.256 --> 13:07.315
Sure. Bets, coffee's right there.

13:07.491 --> 13:10.153
- You just make yourself at home.
- Okay.

13:10.361 --> 13:13.455
- Morning, son.
- Morning, Mom.

13:13.931 --> 13:18.095
I was gonna do a little topless
sunbathing, you're welcome to join me.

13:20.004 --> 13:23.804
Okay, not to put too fine a point on it,
but you're out of your mind.

13:23.974 --> 13:27.910
You need to call a lawyer and get
this marriage annulled immediately.

13:28.245 --> 13:30.770
- I knew you wouldn't understand.
- Oh, I understand.

13:30.948 --> 13:33.610
I understand you're still reeling
from losing Chelsea...

13:33.784 --> 13:37.117
...and you're trying to fill the void
with a menstruating pole dancer.

13:37.288 --> 13:39.483
Hey, hey, that's my wife
you're talking about.

13:39.657 --> 13:41.454
You don't know anything about her.

13:41.625 --> 13:44.753
I know I love her and she loves me
for exactly who I am.

13:44.929 --> 13:48.194
- She doesn't want to change me.
- Oh, stop it.

13:50.301 --> 13:53.031
Okay, you get one of those.

13:53.204 --> 13:55.672
Next time, that hand comes back
a bloody stump.

13:56.674 --> 13:59.871
- Charlie, please, I'm begging you.
- No. I'm doing the right thing.

14:02.046 --> 14:03.809
You're lucky you're not a girl.

14:03.981 --> 14:06.779
Having a hoochie
is like owning a vintage car.

14:06.951 --> 14:11.217
Lot of maintenance and once a month,
you gotta put down an oil pan.

14:14.692 --> 14:16.557
Okay, I may have made a mistake.

14:24.034 --> 14:25.934
Chelsea?

14:27.671 --> 14:29.536
Hey, Charlie.
What are you doing here?

14:29.707 --> 14:32.505
- I need to see your daughter.
- I'm sorry, she's not here.

14:33.010 --> 14:36.138
- Hi, Charlie. What's going on?
- Ed.

14:36.313 --> 14:38.372
- Know when she'll be back?
- I'm not sure.

14:38.549 --> 14:41.712
She took Skipper for a walk.
You're welcome to come in and wait.

14:41.886 --> 14:43.717
Thank you.

14:45.890 --> 14:48.984
- What are you doing?
- I'm just trying to be polite.

14:49.159 --> 14:51.855
Did you consider that maybe
she doesn't want to see him?

14:52.029 --> 14:54.224
Watch your tone, mister.

14:56.166 --> 14:58.031
Sit, please.

14:58.736 --> 15:01.534
Sorry the place is a mess,
we're still decorating.

15:01.705 --> 15:03.935
I'm decorating, he's critiquing.

15:04.575 --> 15:06.839
What? I can have opinions.

15:07.011 --> 15:10.708
He wants me to just shut up
and be pretty.

15:12.249 --> 15:15.685
So listen, I'm sorry things
didn't pan out with you and Chels.

15:15.853 --> 15:17.184
Yeah, me too.

15:17.354 --> 15:19.515
Relationships can be a lot of work.

15:19.690 --> 15:22.181
Even if you've known someone
for 40 years.

15:22.359 --> 15:23.587
That's right.

15:23.761 --> 15:26.093
People get set
in their pigheaded ways.

15:27.865 --> 15:29.730
You wanna get something
off your chest? Hm?

15:29.900 --> 15:31.128
I'm right here.

15:32.236 --> 15:34.761
You really wanna open
this kettle of fish now?

15:34.939 --> 15:36.770
Oh, yeah, let's open it. Open it up.

15:36.941 --> 15:38.806
Okay.

15:39.243 --> 15:42.940
I'm just saying that two grown men
should be able to pick out a club chair...

15:43.113 --> 15:45.274
...without it turning
into lwo-freaking-Jima.

15:45.816 --> 15:49.252
Well, I'm not the one that thinks
that everything he sets his ass on...

15:49.420 --> 15:51.217
...has to be made out of leather.

15:52.656 --> 15:53.714
Lucky for you.

15:55.592 --> 15:57.059
Come on, Skipper.

15:58.495 --> 16:01.089
- Charlie.
- I'm sorry to drop in like this.

16:01.265 --> 16:02.789
I just really needed to see you.

16:03.100 --> 16:04.931
Okay. What's going on?

16:05.302 --> 16:07.566
- Uh, well...
- Why don't we go...

16:07.738 --> 16:09.137
...and leave these two alone?

16:09.306 --> 16:10.739
Fine. Fine.

16:10.908 --> 16:14.810
There's no law that says we can't order
the rug later and get two club chairs.

16:14.979 --> 16:18.176
You see, right there.
That's why I love you.

16:20.918 --> 16:22.852
What are you doing here?

16:23.053 --> 16:24.953
Okay, well...

16:25.122 --> 16:30.082
...I don't know how to say this
except just to say it.

16:30.260 --> 16:33.286
I still love you very much
and I miss you like crazy.

16:33.464 --> 16:34.658
I miss you too, Charlie.

16:34.832 --> 16:35.992
Then what are we doing?

16:36.166 --> 16:39.033
Taking time to figure out
if we're meant to be together.

16:39.203 --> 16:41.330
And how the hell
are we supposed to do that?

16:41.505 --> 16:44.440
I don't know. I guess
we should start dating other people.

16:45.476 --> 16:46.602
What?

16:48.212 --> 16:51.978
I'm not ready to see other people.

16:52.649 --> 16:55.209
I don't know that I am either,
but we have to try.

16:55.386 --> 16:58.844
Chelsea, I can't even think
about dating right now.

16:59.723 --> 17:02.385
Can I tell you something
I've learned since we split up?

17:02.559 --> 17:04.151
Sure. But first, marry me.

17:04.495 --> 17:06.395
- No.
- Okay, just checking.

17:06.597 --> 17:08.963
Probably some
legal complications anyway.

17:09.133 --> 17:11.693
- What?
- Nothing. Nothing. Go ahead.

17:12.036 --> 17:14.527
I learned that I shouldn't have
tried to change you.

17:14.705 --> 17:16.536
You need someone
who loves you for you.

17:16.707 --> 17:19.540
No, no, no. I need to be changed.

17:19.710 --> 17:22.338
There's something seriously wrong
with me.

17:22.513 --> 17:26.381
Please, Chelsea, take me back
and turn me into someone else.

17:27.618 --> 17:30.018
- Wasn't a very good argument, was it?
- Nope.

17:30.888 --> 17:34.255
Well, that's the best I got.

17:36.493 --> 17:40.122
Okay. I guess I should get going.

17:41.198 --> 17:42.722
I'm really sorry.

17:43.400 --> 17:44.992
That's all right.

17:45.169 --> 17:47.501
Say goodbye to your dad and Ed
for me.

17:47.671 --> 17:48.729
I will.

17:49.173 --> 17:50.538
They're a really cute couple.

17:51.508 --> 17:53.840
I guess. It's a little weird for me.

17:54.178 --> 17:57.443
Well, sure, you're probably used to
seeing your dad with your mom...

17:57.648 --> 18:00.014
...and not a big, handsome black guy.

18:01.151 --> 18:02.413
He is handsome.

18:09.359 --> 18:11.088
Hey, Chels...

18:11.795 --> 18:14.059
...I just want you to know
that if by chance...

18:14.231 --> 18:17.029
...you should do something
crazy and stupid...

18:17.201 --> 18:21.661
...like running off
and marrying some stranger...

18:22.439 --> 18:25.101
...I would forgive you
and take you back with open arms.

18:26.043 --> 18:27.237
- Good to know.
- Seriously.

18:27.411 --> 18:29.641
I wouldn't hold it against you at all.

18:30.614 --> 18:31.638
Thank you.

18:33.083 --> 18:34.880
All right then.

18:36.420 --> 18:38.980
- Goodbye.
- Bye.

18:46.230 --> 18:49.597
Stop it, Ed, your beard tickles.

18:50.634 --> 18:53.432
Come on, Skipper,
time for another walk.

19:04.948 --> 19:07.678
- Uh, Charlie, we've got a little problem.
- What's up?

19:07.851 --> 19:09.785
This is Betsy's husband.

19:09.953 --> 19:11.386
Hello.

19:12.656 --> 19:14.624
- Wanna catch me up?
- Really?

19:14.791 --> 19:17.316
Calling him "Betsy's husband"
didn't do the trick?

19:18.028 --> 19:20.553
She never said anything
about being married.

19:20.731 --> 19:22.460
She never does.

19:22.633 --> 19:24.396
- This has happened before?
- Oh, yes.

19:24.568 --> 19:27.128
Any time I find her ring
inside her diaphragm case...

19:27.304 --> 19:29.795
...I know she's off
on one of her little adventures.

19:31.175 --> 19:33.405
- I don't believe this.
- Why do you put up with it?

19:33.810 --> 19:36.142
Look at me.
I'd rather share a girl like Betsy...

19:36.313 --> 19:39.714
...than have an exclusive relationship
with a box of porn magazines.

19:40.184 --> 19:43.153
I hear you. That would be sad.

19:44.021 --> 19:46.546
- Hey, baby.
Hey.

19:47.291 --> 19:49.725
Charlie, I'm really sorry.

19:50.327 --> 19:52.386
I was less than honest with you.

19:53.197 --> 19:56.758
Sure. Let's call it "less than honest."

19:58.368 --> 19:59.995
I did enjoy our honeymoon.

20:00.504 --> 20:01.528
Me too.

20:01.705 --> 20:03.673
Ha, ha. We stayed at Bellagio.

20:04.174 --> 20:05.232
Nice.

20:07.611 --> 20:08.771
Oh, we should go.

20:12.115 --> 20:13.707
- Bye.
- Bye.

20:16.420 --> 20:18.081
I'll make it up to you in the car.

20:18.956 --> 20:22.858
Oh, Betsy,
I'm the luckiest guy in the world.

20:26.396 --> 20:28.330
How about that?

20:28.699 --> 20:30.633
I guess I'm not married.

20:30.834 --> 20:32.859
I guess not.

20:33.237 --> 20:34.568
You know what that means.

20:34.738 --> 20:37.263
Going back to church?

20:41.078 --> 20:44.206
That means I just got three days
of unbelievable sex...

20:44.381 --> 20:46.611
...with no obligations
and no commitment.

20:47.851 --> 20:49.785
Please don't make me slap you again.

20:51.088 --> 20:54.319
No, go ahead.
I think I got one more coming.

20:55.092 --> 20:56.252
That's all right.

20:56.426 --> 20:58.485
I'm happy that things worked out
for you.

20:58.662 --> 21:00.391
Again.

21:00.564 --> 21:01.656
Thanks.

21:01.865 --> 21:05.426
Oh, hey, did I tell you
I won 18 grand in Vegas?

21:07.871 --> 21:09.463
Ouch.
